{
  "_README": "GPU hardware specifications used for roofline (MBU/MFU) analysis. Units: hbm_bandwidth_gbps is in GB/s (1 GB = 1e9 bytes). peak_flops_tflops gives DENSE (not 2:4 sparse) tensor-core throughput in TFLOPS per numeric format; fp4 is the dense FP4 (NVFP4/MXFP4) peak, Blackwell only; null means the format has no tensor-core support on that part. Figures are FP16/BF16 with FP32 accumulate, which is what inference kernels run: professional and datacenter parts run that at full rate, GeForce parts (and the L40) at half rate, and the table carries the achievable (halved) figure for them. GENERATED by scripts/gen_gpu_specs.py from per-SKU SM count, boost clock, bus width and memory data rate using the same formulas the suite applies to a live device (core/hardware/gpu_derive.py); entries whose source is 'datasheet' pin the BF16 peak to NVIDIA's published number where the formula's clock basis differs (Hopper) or the part is cut (H20, A10G, T4, and the RTX PRO Blackwell cards, pinned from NVIDIA's published AI TOPS / 8). Do not edit by hand: edit the SKU list in the script and regenerate. On an NVIDIA host the suite derives the spec from the device and cross-checks this table (see --gpu-spec).",
